# Library typing (ObjectId / S3 / googleapis)

Full guide: `docs/typescript-library-typing-pitfalls.md`.

## Mongoose ObjectId

- Validate with `mongoose.isValidObjectId(id)`, never `Types.ObjectId.isValid` in new code.
- Construct/parse hex ids through `toObjectId` / `isObjectIdString` / `newObjectIdHex` in `src/utils/objectId.ts`, not scattered `createFromHexString` / raw `new mongoose.Types.ObjectId(id)` copies.
- Convert an existing ObjectId with `String(id)`. Do not call `.toHexString()` — TypeScript 6 often types `Types.ObjectId` as a 0-arg class without that method.
- If CI reports `Expected 0 arguments, but got 1` or missing `ObjectId`/statics/`toHexString`, fix via the helper (a typed runtime view of `mongoose.mongo` inside `toObjectId` / `newObjectIdHex`) — do not `@ts-ignore` call sites, and do not use a named `import { ObjectId } from "mongodb"` in serverless route helpers (Vercel has emitted `mongodb_1 is not defined` at runtime).
- `Schema.Types.ObjectId` is for schemas only, not value construction.

## AWS S3

- Call `S3Client.send(new XxxCommand(...))` on the real client.
- If Vercel alone loses the Smithy-inherited `send`, use one generic intersection helper that retains `S3Client` and pairs each command with its real SDK output type.
- Do not invent a dual-overload sender facade; structurally similar commands can resolve to the wrong output.
- `Body` exists on get/read outputs (`GetObjectCommandOutput`), not on `PutObjectCommandOutput`.

## googleapis

- When `google.drive` / `google.sheets` reject `auth` on `Options` or methods return `void` instead of `{ data }`, use the existing cast pattern from `src/services/googleSheets/auth.ts`: `as unknown as drive_v3.Options` / `sheets_v4.Options`, with a short comment.
- Fix client factory and request-body typing first; an explicit method-options argument can prevent selection of a callback/`void` overload.

## Escape hatches

- No `any` / `@ts-ignore` / unexplained double-casts. SDK-boundary casts need a one-line comment naming the library gap.
